**Task 2 — host bearer ACL 14129252: RED (not applied).** `icacls` shows **both** `prodkit_server.py` and `prodkit_chat_secret.json` carry inherited `Everyone:(F)` / `Guest:(M)` / `Authenticated Users:(M)` — world-writable + world-readable. New finding: 5c29124 now **live-reads** the chat bearer secret (`:53/:110/:1312/:1381`); my earlier "316d564 doesn't read it" was vs the old sha — the zeechat merge added the read. So the world-readable bearer becomes load-bearing exactly at this deploy, and the world-writable server file lets any principal swap out the code being gated.

**sha-consistency pin:** deployed `C:/ZeeCloud/prodkit_server.py` lacks all three new markers → currently == live sha 316d564; 5c29124 not yet on disk. Both findings are correctly **pre-launch**.

